lisa-design:
- Round 2 (design §13, R62/R63/R65/R66/R67). API pin: v0.19.1-0.20261001101400-6c801a34ca14 (api#465 round 2, 6c801a3).
- R67 stable path is <state>/inline/<name>/current/bundle, NOT <name>/current: OPA's dirLoader does filepath.Walk(root) with Lstat, so a symlinked ROOT loads zero modules silently (verified on OPA v1.14.1: 0 results; a trailing slash works but breaks under any filepath.Clean). The symlink must be an intermediate component, hence the tree lives at <name>/<digest>/bundle. Pre-R67 <digest> dirs (files directly inside) are rebuilt by writeOnce.
- R67 swap timing: the run loop (reconciler.start) activates only after the previous config's run returned (after the reload drain / kill) and on fallback; never at prepare time (prepare runs while plugins of the old config run; a rejected candidate must never move current). rename-over-symlink is atomic for lookups on Linux only (APFS gives transient EINVAL), and a tree walk across a swap can mix trees, so "only between runs" is the safety argument, not the rename. Activation failure = run failure (fallback or exit).
- R67 identity: candidateIdentity hashes runtime.inlineTrees (digest dirs), never the stable paths (which never change); otherwise a tree change would be adopted without a restart.
- GC/activation share rc.inlineMu; GC keeps active/pending/starting/fallback candidates' trees + the current symlink target. takePending sets rc.starting (cleared by bind) to close the takePending->bind window.
- runner.WithPolicyPaths EvalSymlinks each path at helper creation: evaluation-time bundle artifacts are the tree the run started with even if current is swapped later.
- R62 uploader: runner.ArtifactUploader (exported; plugins import runner) keyed per API base URL (sdk.Client exposes no URL, so callers pass it: apiBaseURL(config) / trimmed api.url, the same string). One instance created in agentRunner() and given to AgentRunner (WithSharedArtifactUploader) and the reconciler (sdkRemote.UploadArtifact). internal/policytree is the single ReadTree/TarFiles (leaf, stdlib only) so runner does not import inlinepolicy/OPA tester.
- R62 uploads happen in maybeReport (report time), not inside prepare: that gives "after checks pass", "mode != off", retry of transient failures on the next report, and no upload for rejected candidates. Memo tree digest -> artifact digest ("" = permanent 4xx other than 404/405/408/429); reset when the remote client is rebuilt (api block change). A tree whose on-disk digest no longer matches (edited local source) is not uploaded.
- R63: the agent does NOT re-run CheckContract on authored modules (regocheck did); static on vendor-only packages, plus duplicate-package-module for authored packages (regocheck can't see vendor modules). Dynamic dry run uses rego.ParsedBundle of sandboxed copies (tests included: test-module rules are part of the evaluated package, parity) + tester stubs as rego options + SandboxCapabilities. Execute aborts on the first package error, so the loop excludes the failing package and retries (bounded by #packages). Dynamic missing-title is downgraded to a warning when a title rule exists (input-dependent), matching static conditional-title. Decode errors get contract codes (invalid-violation / invalid-type) so vendor static+dynamic dedupe by (package, code).
- Dedupe in prepareInline: exact duplicates (static vendor warnings repeat per plugin, carry no plugin prefix) and a warning superseded by an error with the same (bundle, path, code).
- R66 only for plugins that use >=1 inline bundle; non-inline paths are inventoried via sourceInventory (OCI memoized); only non-test compliance_framework.* packages count; the warning is attributed to the inline bundle's file.
